# S. cerevisiae Mating

@left

![Lecture diagram](assets/lect09b-tetrads_1_introduction/image_004.png)

@right

- The yeast _Saccharomyces cerevisiae_ is a simple single celled eukaryote with both a diploid and haploid mode of existence.
- The mating of yeast only occurs between haploids, which can be either the a or &#945; (_alpha_) mating type
- haploid yeast can switch mating type as often as every cell cycle.

